citation: |
  Derived from CMU-1-Small-Region.svs (Aperio, CC0-1.0) via
  wsitools v0.23.0-dev (main @ 6eeb480) `convert --to cog-wsi`: the pyramid is
  re-encoded as a Cloud-Optimized GeoTIFF WSI, and the associated images are
  copied faithfully (verbatim source strips + Predictor/JPEGTables, via
  opentile-go v0.39.0 AssociatedSourceOf) — a LZW + Predictor=2 label, a JPEG
  thumbnail, and a JPEG overview. NOTE: the COG-WSI writer's tile ordering is
  nondeterministic, so regenerating produces a pixel-identical but
  byte-different file; this exact artifact (sha256 above) is the canonical one.
